# ── Claude Code & Council — never commit ───────────────────────────────────
# AI instructions (CLAUDE.md), local agent config, skill artifacts, Council CDRs.
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT ignored (changed 2026-08-11). It used to stand on this line,
# grouped with .claude/ and .claude.json under "never commit" - but that grouping was a
# category error: those are session state and tool config, while CLAUDE.md is the densest
# hand-written documentation in the repo (measured in the Sdk repo: 25 KB, more substance than
# all 37 of its Docs guides combined). Untracked meant no history, no diff, no rollback and -
# the decisive part - no ATOMICITY: one change routinely touches a target, CHANGELOG.md and
# CLAUDE.md, and two of those landed in a commit while the third did not. That is the same
# drift mechanism the 2026-07-15 Harness move was made to stop, and the workspace root already
# decided it this way (its .gitignore re-allows /CLAUDE.md explicitly).
.claude/
.council/
.clauderc
.claude.json
.anthropic/

# ── Security — Keys, Certs, Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────
*.snk
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.private.txt
*.publishsettings
.env
.env.*
[Kk]eys/

# ── Repo-specific ignores and re-includes (keep AFTER the broad ignores) ───
# BenchmarkDotNet run output at the repo root (Evolution-Loop Tier-2 runs).
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# Bootstrap feed: vendored packages so a standalone checkout resolves the
# BuildSdk + Abstractions + TestInfrastructure without the workspace feed
# (see eng/ci/NuGet.CI.config). The workflow that also used them is gone — this
# workspace runs no CI, every gate is local.
!eng/ci/feed/*.nupkg
# eng/keys holds documentation only (no key material) — re-include the README.
!eng/keys/
eng/keys/*
!eng/keys/README.md


# Visual Studio "Stack Trace Explorer" scratch buffers: 0-byte temp editor files VS drops
# in the solution root with a random suffix (e.g. StackTraceExplorerEditor.Fapykil). VS-generated, not ours.
StackTraceExplorerEditor.*
